    "title": "Florida 'revenge' mom found guilty in murder case - NewsBreak",
    "text": "PENSACOLA, Fla. ( WKRG ) — Sheila Agee has been found guilty of principal first-degree premeditated murder for her role in the murder of 18-year-old Brooklyn Sims. After closing arguments from Chief Assistant State Attorney of the First Judicial Circuit Bridgette Myers Jensen and Agee’s defense attorney David Ackerman, the jury deliberated and returned a verdict after about three hours. She has been sentenced to the mandatory minimum of life in prison without the possibility of parole. Sims was shot and killed by her child’s father and Sheila’s son, Keith Agee, while working at Home Depot on Aug. 11, 2023. Text messages presented in court show Sheila corresponded with her son minutes before the murder took place, informing him where Sims was located. “If you don’t come kill her you a mf b**ch,” one text from Sheila to Keith reads. Keith Agee was previously convicted of first-degree premeditated murder in December 2023. He was also sentenced to life in prison without the possibility of parole. After the verdict was read, Sims’ mother, Cornelia Sims was able to read a victim impact statement. “I’ll never be the same. I try to go on for Kasey’s sake,” Sims said in reference to her now 4-year-old granddaughter. “She’s thriving. She’s getting big. Just like Brooklyn from head to toe.” Editor’s Note: Here’s the latest update on this story: Murder suspect’s mother charged after chilling text messages found: Escambia Co. Sheriff’s Office For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
